<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
    <%- include('partials/google-tag') %>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Start-up idea review | Arrington Consultancy</title>
    <%# HIDDEN LANDING PAGE (Tom, 06/10/2026). noindex here and as an
        X-Robots-Tag header from the route. Not in the sitemap, not in the
        navigation, not linked from anywhere else. See routes/startUpReview.js. %>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <meta name="description" content="A £500 set-up review for a start-up idea, from someone who has built, grown and sold real businesses over 20 years in Devon and Cornwall. Starts with a conversation.">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/start-up-idea-review">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Start-up idea review | Arrington Consultancy">
    <meta property="og:description" content="Before you put your money into a start-up, have the idea looked at by someone who has built, grown and sold real businesses.">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/start-up-idea-review">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/img/logo">
    <meta name="csrf-token" content="<%= csrfToken %>">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400&family=DM+Serif+Display&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <%# No Product/Offer schema, deliberately: the page is noindex and the
        offer's deliverables are not yet confirmed. %>
    <style nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        :root {
            <% for (const [prop, val] of Object.entries(theme.vars)) { %>
            <%= prop %>: <%= val %>;
            <% } %>
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body { margin: 0; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; background: var(--black); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-styles') %>

        h1, h2, h3 { font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-weight: 400; color: var(--text-bright); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0; }
        p { color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }

        .btn { display: inline-block; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid transparent; }
        .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--black); border-color: var(--accent); }
        .btn-primary:hover, .btn-primary:focus-visible { background: var(--accent-hover); border-color: var(--accent-hover); }

        main { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; padding: calc(var(--site-chrome) + 2.5rem) 1.5rem 5rem; }

        /* The same page grammar as the sale readiness landing page
           (views/sale-readiness.ejs), which Tom reviewed live on 25/09/2026:
           label, headline, lede, a single primary button, then a de-boxed
           credibility line with hairline rules. Nothing new is invented here. */
        .su-label { font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1rem; display: block; }
        h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 2.4rem); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
        .su-lede { font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--text-bright); margin-bottom: 1.6rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-hero-actions { margin-bottom: 0; }

        .su-cred {
            margin-top: 2.5rem;
            padding: 1.5rem 0;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        }
        .su-cred p { margin: 0; font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--text-bright); }
        .su-cred p + p { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.97rem; }

        .su-section { margin-top: 3.25rem; }
        .su-section > h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
        .su-section > .su-intro { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 1.6rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-section.su-prose > p { max-width: 62ch; }

        /* How the review works: three numbered steps, because this genuinely
           is a sequence (the Ads landing-page standard's "approach" block). */
        .su-card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.9rem 2rem; }
        .su-card > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
        .su-step { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
        .su-step + .su-step { margin-top: 1.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
        .su-step-num { font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 1.6rem; color: var(--accent); opacity: 0.45; line-height: 1; }
        .su-step h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
        .su-step p { font-size: 0.97rem; margin: 0; }
        .su-step p + p { margin-top: 0.6rem; }

        .su-price-row {
            display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.9rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
            margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        }
        .su-price-fig { font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 1.9rem; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
        .su-price-row p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.94rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

        /* Accent-dot list, the site's existing list treatment (Owner Check,
           sale readiness) rather than the browser's default discs. */
        .su-dots { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-dots li { position: relative; padding-left: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--text); }
        .su-dots li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
        .su-dots strong { color: var(--text-bright); font-weight: 700; }
        .su-includes { max-width: none; }
        .su-dots li::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.6em;
            width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent);
        }

        /* Background: directly on the page, a short gold rule under the
           heading, no card (the treatment Tom chose for the sale readiness
           page's closing section on 25/09/2026). */
        .su-section.su-who > h2::after {
            content: ''; display: block; width: 2.5rem; height: 2px; margin-top: 0.9rem; background: var(--accent);
        }
        .su-section.su-who > h2 { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }

        .su-final { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 2.5rem; margin-top: 3.5rem; }
        .su-final h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
        .su-final p { max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-final-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
        .su-aside { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 1.6rem; }
        .su-aside a {
            color: var(--accent);
            text-decoration: none;
            border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent);
            padding-bottom: 2px;
        }
        .su-aside a:hover, .su-aside a:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }
        .su-next { max-width: 62ch; margin-top: 1.1rem; }
        .su-website > p { max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-website > h2 + p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        .su-price-fig-minor { font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-bright); }

        @media (max-width: 760px) {
            main { padding-top: calc(var(--site-chrome) + 1.75rem); }
            .su-section { margin-top: 2.1rem; }
            .su-section > h2 { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
            .su-section > .su-intro { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
            .su-cred { margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.25rem 0; }
            .su-card { padding: 1.4rem 1.25rem; }
            .su-step + .su-step { margin-top: 1.25rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; }
            .su-final { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.9rem; }
            .su-hero-actions .btn, .su-final-actions .btn { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <%# currentPage carries a slug that is deliberately not in navPages: this
        is a hidden campaign landing page (Tom, 06/10/2026), so nothing in the
        nav highlights as active. Header and footer are the site's own. %>
    <%- include('partials/site-header', { currentPage: { slug: 'start-up-idea-review' }, navPages, canEdit: false, content, pageContact }) %>

    <main>
        <%# HERO. The lede is Tom's own description of the offer from his
            brief of 06/10/2026, in "we"-free third person because it is a
            fact about Tom. The proof line is the homepage hero's live proof
            line (content row hero.proof_line, seeded 15/08/2026), with the
            same three items in the same order. Nothing is written for this
            page that is not already approved. %>
        <span class="su-label">Start-up idea review</span>
        <h1>Before you put your money into a start-up, have the idea looked at properly.</h1>
        <p class="su-lede">A £500 set-up review for your start-up idea, from someone who has built, grown and sold real businesses over 20 years in Devon and Cornwall.</p>
        <div class="su-hero-actions">
            <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us about the idea</a>
        </div>

        <div class="su-cred">
            <p>Two decades building, buying and selling businesses. Oxford Saïd, Distinction. 5.0 on Google reviews.</p>
            <p>The owner run businesses we usually work with have been trading for years. This is for the step before that.</p>
        </div>

        <%# APPROACH: the Ads landing-page standard's step block, adapted.
            Three steps because that is the actual sequence. Step 3 points at
            the deliverables block below rather than describing them, because
            the deliverables are Tom's to confirm. %>
        <div class="su-section">
            <h2>How the review works</h2>
            <div class="su-card">
                <div class="su-step">
                    <span class="su-step-num">1</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Tell us about the idea</h3>
                        <p>Use the form at the bottom of this page. What the business would do, who would pay for it, and where you are with it. You do not need a business plan or a pitch deck.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="su-step">
                    <span class="su-step-num">2</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>A straight first conversation, at no charge</h3>
                        <p>We ask the questions we would ask before putting our own money in. If we do not think a paid review would help you, we say so, and you have lost nothing but half an hour.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="su-step">
                    <span class="su-step-num">3</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>The set-up review</h3>
                        <p>If it would help, we go through the idea and the set-up with you properly, for a fixed £500. What that covers is set out below.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <%# WHAT THE £500 SET-UP REVIEW INCLUDES. The four items are Tom's,
            given on 06/10/2026 ("Brand guidance, company structure advice,
            banking advice, accountancy advice", then "Marketing advice" as
            the fifth), in his order. The one-line
            gloss under each says what the item covers in plain words; none
            adds a service, a result or a credential. Tom's first list ended "etc";
            nothing was added for it, and the fifth item is the one he named. The
            accountancy line is deliberately "when you need an accountant"
            rather than accountancy itself: the Brand OS says where the job
            genuinely needs an accountant or a solicitor, use one. %>
        <div class="su-section">
            <h2>What the £500 set-up review includes</h2>
            <div class="su-price-row">
                <span class="su-price-fig">£500</span>
                <p>Fixed. Agreed before any work starts. The first conversation is free.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="su-card">
                <ul class="su-dots su-includes" data-deliverables="5">
                    <li><strong>Brand guidance.</strong> The name, the look and how you describe what you do, settled before you spend money on any of them.</li>
                    <li><strong>Company structure advice.</strong> Sole trader, partnership or limited company, and what each one means for you.</li>
                    <li><strong>Banking advice.</strong> Setting the business up to get paid and to pay out cleanly from day one.</li>
                    <li><strong>Accountancy advice.</strong> What records you need from the start, and when you need an accountant.</li>
                    <li><strong>Marketing advice.</strong> Where your first customers are likely to come from, and what is worth spending on to reach them.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <%# THE WEBSITE BUILD, BELOW THE REVIEW (Tom, 06/10/2026: "slip the
            website build into that page, it needs to sit below the £500
            review, we can build you new website for £999"; wording Tom's of the
            same day: "HTML site a completely customisable non templated
            sites". "Take advantage of our offer" was left out because the
            £999 must never read as a promotion). Its own section,
            directly after the £500 review and visually smaller than it: the
            figure is muted and there is no button, so the review stays the
            page's main offer and the enquiry form its one call to action.
            £999 is the approved public Website Build price
            (lib/whereToStartOffers.js) and must never be framed as a
            reduction. The description line is that offer's approved catalogue
            wording. Both links go OUT to existing pages; nothing on the site
            links IN to this page. %>
        <div class="su-section su-website">
            <h2>A website for your start-up</h2>
            <p>Use our Website Build for your start-up: an HTML site built from scratch, not from a template, and completely customisable.</p>
            <div class="su-price-row">
                <span class="su-price-fig su-price-fig-minor">£999</span>
                <p>Fixed. A recorded planning conversation to agree what it needs to do, a complete first version, and one structured round of changes before launch.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="su-aside su-next">See the <a href="/where-to-start/website-build">Website Build</a>, or how we approach <a href="/websites-and-ai">websites and AI</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <%# HONESTY. The Brand Operating System: "Commercial truth matters
            more than politeness." The point of the review is the judgement,
            and the judgement may be "not as it stands". No promise of
            success, funding or a particular outcome anywhere on the page. %>
        <div class="su-section su-prose">
            <h2>What you will get from us, and what you will not</h2>
            <p>We tell you what we think. That includes telling you if we think the idea is not worth your money as it stands, or needs changing before it is. You are paying for a straight view from someone who has done it, not for encouragement.</p>
            <ul class="su-dots">
                <li>It is not a business plan written for you.</li>
                <li>It is not coaching, and it is not a course.</li>
                <li>It is not advice on raising money, and it is not a promise that the business will work.</li>
                <li>Where the idea needs an accountant, a solicitor or another specialist, we will say which.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <%# BACKGROUND. Both sentences are controlled copy already live on the
            site: the first is the sale readiness page's credibility line
            (approved by Tom on 25/09/2026, from the Business Consultant Devon
            page's own row), the second is the Brand Operating System's PROOF
            wording as published on the same page. Nothing is added. %>
        <div class="su-section su-who">
            <h2>Who you would be talking to</h2>
            <p>Tom Arrington built, grew and sold his own business in a seven-figure exit.</p>
            <p>More than 20 years of experience inside real businesses across Devon and Cornwall sits behind the work.</p>
            <p>The review is a conversation with Tom about your idea. It is not a report generated from a form.</p>
        </div>

        <%# FINAL CALL TO ACTION: a conversation, through the existing footer
            enquiry form (#conversation), which is the only form on the site
            that fires the Contact conversion. No checkout on this page. %>
        <div class="su-final">
            <h2>Tell us about the idea</h2>
            <p>Three or four lines is enough. We reply to arrange a conversation, and we say plainly whether a paid review would be worth your money.</p>
            <div class="su-final-actions">
                <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us about the idea</a>
            </div>
            <p class="su-aside">Prefer to talk? The phone number and WhatsApp are at the bottom of the page.</p>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/site-footer', { canEdit: false, pageContact, content }) %>
    <script nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-script') %>
    </script>
</body>
</html>
